# Review

## Summary

The note makes no cognition claims about models. Its agentive verbs apply to systems, loops and people: "persistence does not decide", "a learning loop must decide which form a lesson belongs in", "the system does the selecting itself", "the system learned". These fall under the conventional-metonymy exception for software systems. "Selecting" and "learned" are also used in the note's declared technical senses: selection-based learning and the broad learning criterion it links. Neither implies internal mental states. No phrase attributes knowing, believing or understanding to a model.
